#!/bin/bash
# A designer's review of what a change looks like, from Claude Opus 5.5 at xhigh
# (Ben, 2026-11-27: any visual design work is reviewed by all three reviewers —
# Antigravity Gemini 4 Neon at xhigh, Codex Astra 6.2 at xhigh, and Claude Opus
# 5.5 at xhigh — while non-visual changes use the agy and codex reviewers).
# Where agy-look hunts what's wrong by a pixel, this judges the design: what
# the eye lands on, hierarchy, rhythm, colour, what looks amateur or
# unfinished, and what to do about each, most important first.
#
#   tools/dev/opus-look [--about "WHAT IT IS, WHAT CHANGED"] PICTURE.png…
#
# PICTUREs: the change's pictures (headless: tools/dev/tsession shot),
# each state, look and scale worth judging, in a folder of yours under
# /var/tmp; whole windows, and crops enlarged where detail matters (it
# can only look: it can't crop for itself). It prints its review and
# writes it to opus-look.md beside the first picture (what it did, to
# opus-look.log). Check each thing it says against the pictures
# yourself, fix what's real, and say in the commit what it found and
# what you did.
#
# The review is the Claude CLI in a child tab (a tmux session where there is
# no Rex pane), as every agent here is (`tools/dev/agents look --by opus`: this
# is that), so it can be read while it looks (`tools/dev/agents peek opus-FOLDER`)
# and told more (`agents say`). Run this in the background: it prints a line a
# minute of what the review is doing, and returns when the review is written (0),
# or as soon as it needs you (3: answer it, then run this again with the same
# pictures to go on waiting). It works from the pictures' folder, not the
# repository, with the tools to read and write files there and no other: nothing
# of the project is loaded, nothing can be run.
exec /usr/bin/python3 "$(dirname "$0")/agents" look --by opus "$@"
